ps://www.thegatewaypundit.com/2026/08/80-page-report-reveals-new-details-about-pharmacy/", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "80-Page Report Reveals New Details About Pharmacy Technicians Involved in Drug Mix-Up That Left Patients Paralyzed at Nashville Hospital", "last_comment_created": 1788015165770, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 3, "score_up": 17, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "An 80-page report revealed more details about a 'pharmacy error' that sent multiple patients into cardiac arrest at a Nashville hospital.", "large_image": "hEkM9OWxYDCbjOYV.png", "title": "80-Page Report Reveals New Details About Pharmacy Technicians Involved in Drug Mix-Up That Left Patients Paralyzed at Nashville Hospital * The Gateway Pundit * by Cristina Laila"}, "post_flair_text": "\ud83d\udca9\u00a0\u00a0POOPY\u00a0\u00a0DAYS", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV3R4j8S", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 202, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "hat", "id": 8804880, "raw_content": "", "author": "PillarOfWisdom", "created": 1787961165429, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "DangerousAmerican76", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.patriots.win", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATV3R4j8S.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.patriots.win/post/KZuiKkBOmTxS.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/BToFXe7Zq9p7AtZR.png", "width": 460, "content-type": "png", "height": 521}], "blurhash": "UPF$YJD%-nWCt:-o-o%g.9%1t6WrpJsmxZRj", "full_resolution": [521, 460]}, "title": "Carry a gun for religious reason", "last_comment_created": 1788013853610, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 3, "score_up": 202, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "SAVE AMERICA", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2093528680555524494", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV3SBCNh", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 91, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8805195, "raw_content": "", "author": "KuzoKevin", "created": 1787976195940, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Litecola2", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATV3SBCNh.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/ItIsHoeMath/status/2093528680555524494", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "\"Healthcare is a human right?\"  You can't call something \"a right\" if someone else has to pay for it. You can't have a right to make somebody do something for you if they don't want to.", "last_comment_created": 1788015331125, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 3, "score_up": 91, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 39, "created": 1787971107000, "id": "2093528680555524494", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1985602728857636864/DGMrFnZO_normal.jpg", "displayName": "hoe_math = PsychoMath", "username": "ItIsHoeMath"}, "content": "@frozenaesthetic Yeah, this one's really easy.\n\nHealthcare costs money. If something costs money, it cannot be a human right.\n\nHere's how that works:\n\nIf healthcare is a human right, does that mean you will pay for my health care? Where can I send my bill? \n\nOh, you don't want to pay for me? Why", "parentTweet": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 0, "created": 1787959103000, "id": "2093478330905346304", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2082154218702450688/QXNSeZPH_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Moon Dragon", "username": "frozenaesthetic"}, "content": "Can people explain what they mean when they say \"healthcare is not a human right\"", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 150}, "likes": 1215}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATV3SCZcr", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 16, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8805695, "raw_content": "Just to get to it - do hospitals intentionally put oxygen sensors on the finger of the arm they have blood pressure cuff on to create low oxygen events to claim issues ?\n\nI have experienced this myself and now with my father in law who is in ICU. \n\nIn my case it was during COVID after a hernia operation - the desperately tried to convince me to be transferred to another hospital because my oxygen was so low.  I realized it was going down every cycle of blood pressure reading - I told them I wanted my oxygen sensor switched to my other hand and my oxygen immediately went from low 80s to mid hi 90\u2019s.  I told them I\u2019m done here and wanted discharged immediately \n\nFast forward to today and I see the same thing happening to my father in law in ICU after a significant car accident. He has been on ventilator for a week - indicating low oxygen. Today just remembered and asked to move oxygen sensor from finger (on same arm as blood pressure monitor) to toe\u2026. Oxygen immediately went from 85-90-95 to 99-100.\n\nWTH ?\n\nSo my question: \nIs this whole placement of oxygen sensors on same arm as blood pressure cuff a tactic to falsely show low oxygen in blood \u2014 as a means to create conditions for other additional and possibly unnecessary care ? ", "author": "carbonsteel", "created": 1788010146290, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Fartnugget", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "A question for any medical professionals on here concerning oxygen level monitoring ", "last_comment_created": 1788013008114, "content": "<p>Just to get to it - do hospitals intentionally put oxygen sensors on the finger of the arm they have blood pressure cuff on to create low oxygen events to claim issues ?</p>\n<p>I have experienced this myself and now with my father in law who is in ICU.</p>\n<p>In my case it was during COVID after a hernia operation - the desperately tried to convince me to be transferred to another hospital because my oxygen was so low.  I realized it was going down every cycle of blood pressure reading - I told them I wanted my oxygen sensor switched to my other hand and my oxygen immediately went from low 80s to mid hi 90\u2019s.  I told them I\u2019m done here and wanted discharged immediately</p>\n<p>Fast forward to today and I see the same thing happening to my father in law in ICU after a significant car accident. He has been on ventilator for a week - indicating low oxygen. Today just remembered and asked to move oxygen sensor from finger (on same arm as blood pressure monitor) to toe\u2026. Oxygen immediately went from 85-90-95 to 99-100.</p>\n<p>WTH ?</p>\n<p>So my question:\nIs this whole placement of oxygen sensors on same arm as blood pressure cuff a tactic to falsely show low oxygen in blood \u2014 as a means to create conditions for other additional and possibly unnecessary care ?</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 8, "score_up": 16, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV3SC0zm", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 33, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "stable", "id": 8805416, "raw_content": "", "author": "TiggerLovingPooh", "created": 1787995842101, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "hazelknut", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATV3SC0zm.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/dtlHc2M4l6eJ.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/W5aVAHiXBENsCE2l.png", "width": 535, "content-type": "png", "height": 446}], "blurhash": "UuK^~gay%goL%MayWBay~qWBM{fkRiWBoLoL", "full_resolution": [446, 535]}, "title": "MISSION ACCOMPLISHED", "last_comment_created": 1788004072676, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": true, "comments": 3, "score_up": 33, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0,